cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ReproLLM in your research, please cite it and include the
  generated REPRODUCIBILITY.md with your artifact.
title: ReproLLM
type: software
authors:
  - name: ReproLLM maintainers
repository-code: "https://github.com/EnumaElish123/ReproLLM"
url: "https://github.com/EnumaElish123/ReproLLM"
abstract: >-
  A reproducibility linter, experiment recorder, lockfile system, and drift
  detector for LLM research. It records the LLM-specific state that other
  tools ignore — model revision, tokenizer and chat-template hashes, prompt
  hashes, generation parameters, LLM-as-a-Judge configuration, and the
  pinnability of closed-source API models — and tells you why two runs differ.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - llm
  - research
  - audit
  - lockfile
license: Apache-2.0
